{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.215.060","page_type":"section"},"citation":"18.215.060","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.215.060","content_hash":"8e4c8b6a8fa1768fc078ba5c3a1d899373ea8ab7e6aa6a8f23c8d51251b95ca5","heading":"Revocation.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.215.060:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.215.060","text":"(a) The Planning Commission may recommend revocation of a conditional use permit to the Governing Body; provided, that the Commission has notified in writing the property owner and has given the property owner an opportunity to appear before the Planning Commission.\n(b) Revocation may occur if any of the following applies:\n(1) Failure to comply with any of the conditions established in the permit;\n(2) The use has expanded or deviated from its original use and purpose; or\n(3) The use has been found by a court of law, Federal or State agency to be an illegal activity or nuisance.\n(c) The Planning Commission shall submit its recommendation to the Governing Body which will decide in accordance with K.S.A. 12-757(d) and amendments thereto. (Ord. 19691 § 6, 1-17-12.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"592c7d9b-977a-5e24-a2a6-9470e1ca57cd"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.215.060","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.215.060","content_hash":"ae9e2b5d47f6b9a0996e58bc6a9ff4de9dda58c34f5bd43bc505f2a79917dff9","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.215.060:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.215.060:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/